Wiki Page tables, follow-up of the width model review: a column delete on a table with a custom width but no stored column widths (set by the handle of #824) takes the deleted column's rendered width off the table instead of stretching the remaining columns; a drag on a step table clamped to the page no longer shows the stored column widths for one frame when it starts; a width drag follows only the pointer that started it; the first column's offset is measured also when every row has a merged cell; one shared cell width style for the editor and the view. https://gitlab.kitconcept.io/kitconcept/distribution-kitconcept-intranet/-/work_items/836 @reekitconcept
